comments[21]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-03T11:08:05.494Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check 2026-08-03: searched all statuses for session topic automatic infer provenance, infer session topic from work items, automatic session role detection, agent session semantic attribution, and semantic session topic role claimed work inference. Closed pm-rbg1qo owns declaration and propagation, open pm-eq9dlw owns the invalid boolean role signal, open pm-lu6sca owns resolver outcome semantics, and open pm-1wiugq owns corpus coverage instrumentation; none owns automatic semantic inference from claimed work."
  "2026-08-03T11:11:51.123Z","harness:codex","Correction 2026-08-03: the first create-time census statement incorrectly said role coverage was zero. The exact post-mutation all-history projection is 43,787 events: model 0, effort 702, role 37, topic 0. Current description and why-now now carry the corrected values; immutable history preserves both the error and this correction."
  "2026-08-04T09:18:06.053Z","harness:codex","Fresh semantic-attribution evidence 2026-08-04: a no-override Codex plan mutation records harness and instance automatically but no role or topic. The claimed audit plan already supplies a bounded semantic source for both fields, so the absence is observable on the exact workflow this feature targets. No per-command author or environment override was needed or used."
  "2026-08-08T08:10:42.288Z","harness:claude-code","Reproduced live on 2026-08-08 against pm-cli 2026.8.7, HEAD build. agent_provenance in a create recorded this session resolves model {claude-opus-5, probe}, effort {xhigh, environment} and version {2.1.226, probe}, and leaves topic null outright — no value, no source key, so a consumer cannot distinguish a harness that cannot supply a topic from a resolver that ran and found nothing, which is the ambiguity pm-lu6sca owns generally. Four of five provenance dimensions now resolve automatically without any identity flag; topic is the remaining gap alongside the role defect pm-eq9dlw owns. Evidence is the last history entry of pm-3lhth4."
  "2026-08-08T22:13:15.052Z","harness:codex","Implementation start 2026-08-09: active in the coupled context-provenance tranche with pm-3zgh2c, pm-eq9dlw, pm-lu6sca, pm-b1w8vr, and pm-h75tjh. Scope is SDK-first provenance inference and resolver outcomes, typed role domains, stable entity read-back projections, and epoch-aware release classification; all other open items remain unclaimed."
  "2026-08-08T22:32:58.192Z","harness:codex","TDD evidence: focused contract run initially failed on the legacy role expectation and exact history shape after introducing controlled roles and explicit provenance outcomes; implementation and assertions were corrected, then the five focused suites passed 152/152."
  "2026-08-08T23:34:19.309Z","harness:codex","Tranche pause: bounded role/topic inference and public diagnostics primitives landed, but this broader feature remains open because canonical claimed/focused lineage inference, transport-wide equivalence, scale budgets, corpus coverage ratchets, and graded relevance evaluation are not yet complete."
  "2026-08-09T00:09:12.678Z","harness:codex","Broad tranche evidence: semantic argv roles/topics, bounded diagnostic outcome states, privacy-safe failed-attempt history context, health aggregation, and public SDK exports now pass the complete 7086-test 100/100/100/100 gate. Item remains open and unclaimed because the remaining canonical-lineage, transport-equivalence, scale/eval, and ratchet acceptance criteria are outside this completed tranche."
  "2026-08-09T00:20:21.889Z","harness:codex","Delivery handoff: broad SDK/CLI tranche committed at 5b36abc75 and opened as GitHub PR #944 (https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/pull/944). Exact local evidence includes 7,086 tests across 461 files at 100/100/100/100 coverage, package/compatibility/npx/dogfood/manual acceptance, tracker/changelog/SDK/static-quality gates, and zero current dependency or GitHub security alerts. Review and exact-head CI evidence will be appended after the hosted loop."
  "2026-08-09T00:43:38.878Z","harness:codex","Review clarification: implementation evidence dated 2026-08-09 uses the Europe/Vienna local evidence date (UTC+02:00). Immutable history timestamps remain canonical UTC, so 2026-08-08T22:13:15.052Z is the same instant as 2026-08-09T00:13:15.052+02:00."
  "2026-08-09T01:24:45.210Z","harness:codex","PR #944 hosted evidence for the completed tranche portion: implementation commit b6678b8 passed all deterministic checks; all 16 CodeRabbit findings are addressed, replied to, and resolved. Item stays open and unclaimed for its broader remaining semantic attribution acceptance."
  "2026-08-10T12:25:39.000Z","harness:claude-code","Provenance baseline measured 2026-08-10 from a live mutation, so this item's remaining scope is now precise rather than inherited.\nRead directly off the newest history entry of a freshly created item, with no PM_AUTHOR set and no --author passed anywhere in the session:\nauthor            harness:claude-code\nauthor_source     detected\nagent_harness     claude-code\nagent_model       claude-opus-5      source probe\nagent_instance    b006a2086429d635675530d7\nagent_provenance  effort  xhigh        source environment\nrole    implementer  source argv\ntopic   pm-ob9z4y    source argv\nversion 2.1.226      source probe\nSo harness, model, thinking effort and harness version are all resolved automatically and correctly, and the role dimension no longer records the boolean child-session flag that pm-eq9dlw was filed for — it reads implementer. Every field carries its own source, which is the property that makes the remaining gap legible instead of guessable.\nWhat is left is exactly the semantic half this item names, and the source labels prove it. role and topic both read source argv. topic resolves to the id of the item the command happened to mutate, and role to a value inferred from the command shape. Both are mechanical proxies: they are correct as provenance and wrong as attribution. A session that touches forty items records forty different topics, none of which is the session's subject, and a session that reviews rather than implements still records implementer because the verb it used was an update.\nThe consequence for the record is that topic and role cannot be aggregated. Grouping history by topic yields one bucket per item, so the question this dimension exists to answer — what was this session about, and in what capacity was the agent acting — is unanswerable even though the field is populated. A null would at least be honest; an argv echo reads as adopted while behaving as absent, which is the same failure shape pm-pcys9n recorded for the release field.\nTwo constraints for the inference this item will add. It must not overwrite a probe-sourced or environment-sourced value, since those are ground truth and the semantic layer is not. And it must record its own source distinctly, so an inferred topic is never mistaken for a declared one; source inferred alongside the existing probe, environment and argv vocabulary."
  "2026-08-10T12:57:05.390Z","harness:codex","Implementation start 2026-08-10: active in the coupled semantic context traceability tranche with pm-f86lth and pm-tld20c. Scope includes canonical claimed/focused lineage inference, bounded explainable provenance, transport parity, coverage/evaluation gates, and privacy-safe evidence; all other items remain unclaimed."
  "2026-08-10T13:53:43.174Z","harness:codex","Implementation evidence: claim/release/focus now maintain a bounded privacy-safe semantic workset keyed by agent instance or author hash; inferred v2 role/topic provenance has strict precedence below declarations, malformed state fails open, and pm context consumes the same claim/focus/lineage affinity without increasing its token budget. Focused build and 38-test transport/provenance suite pass."
  "2026-08-10T14:30:43.660Z","harness:codex","Final verification evidence 2026-08-10: linked PM tests passed 40/40 across the agent runtime, semantic session attribution, provenance ratchet, and context relevance suites. The complete sandboxed repository run passed 470 files and 7,154 tests at exact 100% statements (51,245/51,245), branches (37,511/37,511), functions (10,528/10,528), and lines (49,553/49,553), with zero uncovered counts. Isolated pnpm lint passed ESLint, zero jscpd clones, 100% source/export/member docstrings, package and SDK boundaries, surface replication, token budgets, context calibration, tracker measurement, SDK import costs, and CLI transport floors. Context evaluation produced NDCG, reciprocal rank, required recall, continuity, and token-budget adherence of 1.0 while preserving the existing ceiling; negative controls failed as intended. Secrets scan and pnpm audit found no credential-like tracked secrets and no known vulnerabilities."
  "2026-08-10T14:30:44.178Z","harness:codex","Manual isolated acceptance 2026-08-10: built dist CLI initialized a fresh temporary project, created a Decision -> Feature -> Task lineage, claimed and focused the Feature without topic/role flags, and persisted one private semantic entry with planner/high attribution, the active claim, and bounded claim/focus/lineage evidence. pm context retained all three active lineage items inside a 256-token ceiling, marked selection complete, and assigned the claimed Feature a nonzero claim_focus contribution. No prompt text, arbitrary session content, filesystem path, credential, or raw payload was retained in semantic state."
  "2026-08-10T14:37:36.800Z","harness:codex","Packaged closeout: package artifact gate passed @unbrained/pm-cli 2026.8.10 with 1,343 files and no forbidden sourcemaps; packed npx smoke passed across all 13 packages; package-first dogfood executed 88 commands successfully. Changelog generation via current pm-changelog 2026.8.7 is idempotent and includes this feature under Unreleased."
  "2026-08-10T14:39:49.249Z","harness:codex","Delivery evidence: commit 23c24b111 is published in GitHub PR #965 (https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/pull/965), with the canonical item linked directly in the PR description. Hosted exact-head checks, review inventory, merge, and post-merge release/telemetry proof will be appended separately."
  "2026-08-10T14:43:24.843Z","harness:codex","Hosted CI correction: PR #965 Gates (static) identified the generated full contract snapshot as stale at its first semantic surface difference. Regenerated tests/fixtures/contracts/full.json from the exact build; pnpm contracts:check now passes locally. No runtime contract changed beyond the already reviewed additive surface."
  "2026-08-10T14:54:38.613Z","harness:codex","Hosted coverage correction: all four PR #965 shards passed but their merged map exposed the persisted-null early fail-open branch at src/core/session/session-state.ts:58, which the local monolithic order had covered incidentally. Added a direct real-file null attribution regression in the already linked semantic session suite. Fresh complete run passes 470 files and 7,154 tests at exact 100/100/100/100 with zero uncovered counts."
  "2026-08-10T15:03:01.955Z","harness:codex","Hosted exact-head evidence for PR #965: head 41add6caba2ce3c43aa2f457fcedccdc1fc33641 passed build foundation, static, typecheck, compatibility, smokes, four coverage shards plus aggregate exact-100 gate, Codecov patch, CodeQL, Semgrep, Trivy, TruffleHog, actionlint, ShellCheck, PSScriptAnalyzer, Windows/macOS/Linux runtime, docs, benchmarks, DeepScan, CodeFactor, Hound, and CodSpeed. Final review inventory found zero threads and no actionable findings. Every bot comment/review was reacted to and dispositioned. Greptile emitted no response; CodeRabbit and Sourcery review execution reported provider rate limits, recorded as limitations rather than approval."
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-09T20:05:23.856Z","harness:claude-code","Corpus census of the provenance block, taken 2026-08-09 evening over every history stream in the tracker. This is the coverage measurement this item's gate criterion calls for, taken once by hand so the criterion has a baseline to ratchet from.\n\nPopulation: 46,439 history entries, of which 6,893 carry a provenance block at all, which is 14.8 percent. Within those 6,893, the dimensions populate at four different rates and none of them is close to complete. Model is set on 284 entries, 4.1 percent, always from a probe source. Version is set on the same 284. Effort is set on 986, 14.3 percent, always from the environment. Role is set on 407, 5.9 percent. Topic is set on 425, 6.2 percent.\n\nThe finding this item exists for is in the topic distribution, and it is sharper than the null it was filed against. Topic is no longer null — it is populated, and every one of the 425 populated values came from the argv source, and all 39 distinct values are item identifiers. The field named for the session's subject is being filled with the object of the individual invocation. This is worse than null for the purpose the criterion states, because a null topic is visibly absent and an argv-derived one is invisibly wrong: any consumer grouping work by topic gets one group per item touched rather than one group per session, and the grouping looks successful. A coverage gate that measures non-null topic rates would score this as progress.\n\nThe related role finding is legacy and must not be re-filed. Role carries the literal value 1, from the environment, on 264 entries, and the separate value implementer, from argv, on 143. The 264 boolean-valued rows run from 2026-08-03 to 2026-08-08 and stop there; pm-eq9dlw closed on 2026-08-09 with a resolution that added bounded corpus-wide value-domain scanning reporting these as legacy. No boolean-valued role has been minted since that fix, so the closure is sound and the rows are immutable history, not an escape.\n\nTwo consequences for this item's acceptance criteria, neither of which changes their wording. The criterion requiring a versioned controlled vocabulary inferred from claim state rather than copied from an environment flag is confirmed as still unmet on the topic dimension as well as the role dimension, and for the same underlying reason: a dimension is being filled from whatever nearby value is syntactically available rather than from evidence about the session. And the corpus-facing coverage gate the criterion requires should measure per-dimension non-null rate broken down by source, not just by harness, because a gate blind to source would have reported topic coverage rising from zero to 6.2 percent and called it progress on exactly the day the wrong value started being written.\n\nMethod note for whoever implements the gate: the block is per-entry and optional, so the denominator question is live here in the same shape horizon AI describes. Coverage over entries carrying a block is 6.2 percent for topic; coverage over all entries is 0.9 percent. The gate must declare which denominator it speaks for."
